%=====================================================================%
In this experiment, we try replacing the multi-head attention with mean pooling, or simple attention to verify its effectiveness in the previewing-aware attention. 
The mean pooling regards input segments equally, calculating the average of segment features.
The simple attention utilizes an FC layer to learn attention weights, where we first concatenate the preview feature with the input segment feature vectors, and an FC layer is employed to map each feature vector into an attention weight.
Two attentions are consistently better than the mean pooling, showing the benefit of attention in video representation.
Besides, we find that replacing the multi-head attention with the simple attention would result in relative performance degeneration, but not dramatically. It not only reflects the effectiveness of the multi-head attention, but also shows the robustness of our model structure.



